nd `src/implement-graph.ts` own the closed v2 commands, stable run/delivery identity, owner-private SQLite journal, repository-external state-root safety, canonical `ImplementPlanV2`, and static/dynamic readiness proof.\n- Worker routing and HTTP boundary: `src/route-policy.ts`, `src/worker-broker.ts`, `src/parent-provider.ts`, `skills/_shared/load-config.mjs` with `skills/_shared/load-config.d.mts`, `skills/_shared/http-client.mjs`, `config/routes.example.json`, and `config/.env.example` own whole-file route policy, bounded health/failover/rebind, inherited/custom Provider composition, non-secret provenance, and research HTTP configuration.\n- Research skills: `skills/context7-auto-research/` and `skills/grok-search/`; commit skill: `skills/git-commit/`.\n- Child execution: `src/child-session.ts` owns disposable in-memory sessions, stable task/phase submission identity, safe one-result classification, and cancellation; `src/scoped-tools.ts` confines read/grep/find/ls to admitted paths; `src/empty-resource-loader.ts` supplies no discovered resources; `src/parent-payload-bridge.ts` owns generation/model-bound parent callback capture and lifecycle invalidation; package Agents remain read-only candidate/evidence producers.\n- Artifact and workspace execution: `src/artifact-store.ts`, `src/workspace-store.ts`, `src/isolation-backend.ts`, `src/task-ledger.ts`, `src/candidate-preflight.ts`, `src/patch.ts`, `src/file-snapshot.ts`, and `src/safe-path.ts` own sealed candidate bytes, immutable revisions, Bubblewrap isolation, durable phase/repair facts, strict isolated verification, exact diff admission, currentness, and component-wise no-symlink observation.\n- Workflow authority: `src/workflow-engine.ts` is the sole v2 transition authority for delivery admission, durable readiness/queueing, baselines, Red-Green-Refactor, cumulative attribution and bounded repair, parent-owned tracking/AGENTS operations, final apply, resume/rebind/cancel/discard, recovery, and truthful completion. `src/apply-transaction.ts` owns currentness-checked journaled main-workspace application; `src/index.ts` owns verified prompt activation, v2 tool registration, package delivery loading, and the bounded bootstrap selector. `src/runtime.ts`, `src/worker.ts`, `src/scheduler.ts`, and `src/drain.ts` contain only the selector-isolated one-time v1 bootstrap branch, which becomes unreachable after the durable v2 handoff.\n- TUI presentation: `src/subagent-activity.ts` owns width-safe interactive activity projection and compact terminal metadata; nonterminal queued/connecting/waiting-first-response/running/validating/retrying/verifying/paused/approval-needed/applying/recovering states never render as completed, operation-cancelled is not run success, discarded/rejected are non-success terminal states, and active display/timer state is not persisted.\n- Structural delivery: `src/submit-tool.ts` accepts one final typed result or sealed candidate protocol; `src/result-store.ts` retains exact legacy-bootstrap diff bytes only in memory; `src/verification-capability.ts` validates shell-free Vitest, package-script, static, and ordered-step adapters; `src/contracts.ts` owns strict evidence/diff envelopes and closed safe failure codes.\n  Child code never imports parent apply or state authority.\n- Standalone commands: `bun run check`, `bun run lint`, `bun run test`, `bun run test:target <files>`, `bun run check:agents`, `bun run pack:check`, `bun run traceability:check`, `bun run verify` (check && lint && test && pack:check), and fresh-process seed acceptance `bun scripts/seed-acceptance.mjs`.\n  Distribution: `provenance/adapted-modules.yaml` pins package-shipped Agent identity; `scripts/pack-check.mjs` verifies the real 59-member tarball and `scripts/traceability-check.mjs` verifies all 162 active Requirement/Scenario entries resolve and are owned exactly once.\n- The relocated reference repository is read-only implementation, attribution, license, and provenance evidence; 